    "notes": [
      "Automatic detection and catalog matching were not run.",
      "Pixel values and stretch limits are IMAGE - ZODI (SPHEREx zodiacal model subtracted) in MJy/sr; PNGs use an asinh mapping with the same contrast for every frame of a detector, and transparent pixels mean no data. Saturated star cores and detector-defect pixels are filled from their neighbours for display only; they count as invalid in valid_fraction.",
      "Frame selection: downloaded 80 candidate frame(s) (up to 2 x max_frames=40) and kept 40, spread round-robin over seasons x detectors; inside each (season, detector) the frames whose wavelength at the field centre is closest to a per-detector reference (D1 0.869 um, D2 1.505 um, D3 1.740 um, D4 2.498 um, D5 4.175 um, D6 4.508 um) come first, then those nearest the season middle; frames without a known wavelength rank last. Rejected 2 bad frame(s) whose IMAGE - ZODI robust scatter exceeds 15x the noise of their VARIANCE plane (background steps). Downloaded 75 more D2/D3 frame(s) only to find J/H/Ks wavelengths for the false-color composites; they are not blink frames.",
      "False-color composites: 4 'detectors' and 3 'jhk' season composite(s) (infrared, not true color). detectors = full range: blue = D1 (fallback D2), green = D3 (D4), red = D6 (D5), coadds of the season's published frames. jhk = 2MASS-like: blue / green / red = coadd of the season's downloaded exposures (including unpublished candidates) within 0.06 um of J 1.25 / H 1.65 / Ks 2.17 um at the field centre, else the nearest one within 0.12 um. Each channel: one weight per frame, sky removed, bad pixels left out (saturated cores drawn white, for display only). Green spans 2 sigma below the sky to the bright end of its usable pixels; red and blue are scaled to green by the median field-star flux ratio (target halo excluded), so typical field stars look white; limits shared by every season with the same detectors; colour-preserving asinh (Lupton et al. 2004). Skipped: jhk S0: no exposure within 0.12 um of red (Ks 2.17 um); nearest 2.376 um.",
      "Skipped 2 frame(s): 2025W17_4B_0468_1D1: bad frame: noise 45.5x VARIANCE; 2025W17_4B_0468_2D1: bad frame: noise 24.6x VARIANCE"
    ]
